arith_loop	benchmarks/rebus/arith_loop.reb runs clean, deterministic, output 45000150000 -- independently verified (sum 1..300000 = n(n+1)/2). No benchmark-additive absorption path exists yet in util_build_rungs_suite.py (scoped to corpus/tests/<lang>/ only; the "master-builder-absorbs-demos-benchmarks-programs-and-loose-pairs-additively" extension has not landed). Every language's benchmarks/ tree shows the same gap (census: snobol4 38 owed, prolog 141, icon 36, pascal 11, raku 17) -- cross-language infrastructure, not rebus-specific. Parked here with its verified answer on record. ⛔ NOTE (seat14, same sitting): util_build_rungs_suite.py --lang rebus unconditionally REWRITES this whole file from its own KEEP.md/PENDING.md-derived list every run, discarding any hand-added line like this one -- see the FINDING above filed to hq_T. Re-verify this line is still present after any future run of that tool for rebus.
